# Cloudflare Workers Redirects
# Remove trailing slashes and handle clean URLs

# Cache manifest, sitemap (cache handled by _headers file)
/manifest.webmanifest  /manifest.webmanifest  200
/robots.txt  /robots.txt  200
# NOTE: no self-rewrite for /sitemap.xml - functions/sitemap.xml.js serves it
# (static sitemap + admin-published blog URLs). A self-rewrite would shadow it.

# Clean URLs are handled automatically by Cloudflare Pages (serves *.html for /path).
# NOTE: Do NOT add manual 200-rewrites for .html files - they conflict with Pages'
# built-in clean URL handling and cause infinite 308 redirect loops.

# Trailing slash removal — redirect /page/ to /page
# NOTE: directory pages (/home, /pain-oil, /shilajit contain index.html) must NOT
# have /* -> path rules: Pages auto-308s /path to /path/ and it infinite-loops.
/about-us/*  /about-us  301
/contact-us/*  /contact-us  301
/disclaimer/*  /disclaimer  301
/privacy-policy/*  /privacy-policy  301
/refund-policy/*  /refund-policy  301
/shipping-policy/*  /shipping-policy  301
/terms-and-conditions/*  /terms-and-conditions  301
/thank-you/*  /thank-you  301

# 404 catch-all — return 404 with Cloudflare's default page
# (Cloudflare Workers Pages handles 404s automatically for unmatched routes)

# Shortcuts
/buy     /#checkout    301
/order   /#checkout    301
# /thank-you handled by Workers clean URL (auto serves thank-you.html)

# Duplicate homepage removed — /home now sends everyone to the real homepage (/).
# NOTE: exact rules only — /home/assets/* must keep serving the shared image folder.
/home     /    301
/home/    /    301

# Redirect old shop.html to homepage - contains old Purchase tracking code
/shop.html  /  301

# Old duplicate Shilajit page -> canonical PDP (duplicate content + stale schema)
/shilajitpro  /shilajit/  301
/shilajitpro/*  /shilajit/  301

# SECURITY: never publish local dev secrets. `.dev.vars` lives in the repo root
# for `wrangler dev`; Pages uploads it even though .gitignore lists it, so it was
# publicly downloadable. Redirect every request away from it.
/.dev.vars  /  301
/.dev.vars/*  /  301
/.env  /  301
/.env.local  /  301
